From 96b5e22d5f140ae4d94e4c0ee71bf438474cf08c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Harada <lucasharada51@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 17:06:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] fix(parser): handle full Showdown replay downloads +
 descriptive errors

The UI passes the pasted replay as raw text. When a full replay download
(which carries its battle log under "log") was pasted as JSON, the string
branch went straight to the structured-JSON handler and raised
"Replay contains no sides/teams". Now the string branch decodes JSON and
delegates to the dict path, which detects the "log" field and parses the
battle log.

Also:
- Attribute observed moves to the mon named on the |move| line instead of
  the last active mon (fixes doubles).
- Make parser errors descriptive and actionable (invalid JSON position,
  the top-level keys that were present, what shapes are accepted, and a
  first-line hint for raw logs).
- Surface the error category + a tip in the Streamlit UI.
- Add regression tests for full replay downloads and for the descriptive
  error messages.
---
