From 0758298b2d1412227f1cfeb936e9b8a7a109d007 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Harada <lucasharada51@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 20:37:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] feat(analysis): battle-result context, cross-side
 selection, Chaos name resolution, data docs

Improves analysis quality and metagame explainability:

- Parser extracts the battle OUTCOME from the log (winner, per-turn faints,
  rosters brought). GameState gains outcome/side_of/brought_by_player.
- The explanation AI now receives battle_result (ground truth) and is told to
  anchor on what actually happened and critique poor picks/leads instead of
  advising fainted Pokemon.
- Selection enforces CROSS-SIDE matchups only (never pairs two Pokemon from the
  same roster) and is prompted with per-side rosters + the result.
- Chaos and Smogon adapters resolve species names case/forme-insensitively
  (Typhlosion-Hisui, Metagross-Mega, ...), so real usage files populate.
- Expanded the sample Chaos file to cover this game's species; UI shows the
  battle result and warns when no metagame data is loaded.
- Adds DATA.md + data/ layout documenting where scraped meta/Chaos JSON goes.
- New tests for outcome extraction, cross-side guardrail and name resolution.
