From e9e939ff090588bc7c842f856824fe5ab3bc436f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Harada <lucasharada51@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 21:48:39 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] feat(parser): ordered action timeline to prevent
 hallucinated causality

The battle outcome previously exposed only faints (turn + species), so the
explanation AI invented turn order and causality (e.g. claiming Pyroar attacked
and KO'd Typhlosion when Pyroar actually fainted turn 1 without acting and
Typhlosion fell to Venusaur's Earth Power turn 2).

The parser now reconstructs the exact ORDERED timeline of actions: each move
(actor, target, damage %, effectiveness, spread, crit, miss) and switch, with
faints attributed to the move that caused them. GameState.outcome gains an
'events' list; outcome_summary renders it as a strict, ordered timeline. The
explanation prompt now forbids inventing order/causality and states that a
Pokemon with no 'used' line before fainting did not act.

Adds regression tests asserting Pyroar never acted, Typhlosion's faint is
attributed to Earth Power, and the timeline is ordered.
