From 53d4aee078e58b39a49e0f609f0e164dd6a55c66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Harada <lucasharada51@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 21:59:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] feat(context): metagame context covers ALL in-play
 Pokemon, not just the focus

Previously meta_context and Smogon strategies were built from
selection.focus_species (the 1st AI's picks, typically the turn-1 leads), so the
AI only saw Chaos data for a subset. Now both are built over context_species():
every Pokemon brought by BOTH sides during the game, unioned with any focus. The
selection focus still drives which matchups get the deterministic calc.

Adds a regression test asserting both sides' in-play Pokemon appear in the meta
context and strategies even when the selection focus is deliberately narrow.
