From 634d898fc00e44e9960145d0f72a91d47f4a5d9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Harada <lucasharada51@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 22:11:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] feat(calc): field-aware speed/damage (Tailwind,
 paralysis, Trick Room, weather)

Fixes hallucinated speed order. The speed comparison ignored the field, so the
AI wrongly claimed a Tailwind-boosted Pokemon was outsped.

- Parser extracts a FieldConditions ledger from the log: Tailwind windows per
  side, Trick Room windows, weather, and per-Pokemon status (par/brn/...).
- The Node engine computes effective speed via @smogon/calc getFinalSpeed
  (Tailwind, paralysis, Choice Scarf, weather abilities); the adapter inverts
  move order under Trick Room and labels the conditions applied.
- MatchupEvaluator builds the field spec per matchup (Tailwind for the side that
  had it, Trick Room, weather) and feeds it to both damage and speed calcs;
  observed status is applied to the sets.
- SpeedComparison.faster now means 'moves first' and carries conditions; the
  timeline annotates active field conditions per turn; the prompt forbids
  asserting speed order against the timeline/verdicts.

Adds field-condition tests. 49/49 passing.
