Subject: [PATCH 6/8] feat(chaos): rating-tier selection + regulation fallback
 for meta context

Fixes empty metagame/strategy sections and adds elo-aware context.

- New ChaosRepository indexes a directory of Chaos files named
  <metagame>-<ratingCutoff>.json. It selects the IDEAL tier (highest cutoff,
  used for suggestions) and the CURRENT tier (the bracket the match rating falls
  into), and walks a regulation-fallback chain (same game only, up to 3 regs)
  when a species is absent from the newest regulation.
- ChaosAdapter/ChaosStrategyAdapter now source data through the repository and
  tag each summary with its source (incl. '(fallback)'). MetaContext gains
  current_tier_stats and rating_note; PokemonMetaSummary gains source.
- Parser extracts the match rating; services pass metagame+rating through.
- Sample tier files (regmb 0/1500/1630/1760) + a previous reg (regma) added
  under data/chaos to demonstrate tiers and fallback; config points there.
- Prompt explains ideal vs current tier and fallback sources. DATA.md documents
  the naming convention and logic. Adds repository/fallback tests. 55/55 passing.
