From: Lucas Harada <lucasharada51@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 23:17:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] feat(analysis): per-turn ground-truth verification +
 stronger forme resolution

Adds the turn-by-turn feedback loop the whole-game summary lacked.

- TurnReplaySimulator re-consults the deterministic engine for EVERY move
  actually used: projected damage of that move vs the real target under THAT
  turn's field conditions (Tailwind/Trick Room/weather/status), the field-aware
  speed order, and the logged actual result (remaining HP or KO). Status/setup
  moves are flagged as non-damaging.
- TurnCheck/TurnDamageCheck domain models; AnalysisResult.turn_checks; both
  pipelines populate it and pass turn_by_turn_checks into the explanation context.
- Prompt instructs the AI to walk the game turn by turn and compare projected vs
  actual (noting projections assume default EVs/base forme).
- ChaosRepository forme resolution now trims trailing forme segments
  progressively (Raichu-Mega-Y -> Raichu-Mega -> Raichu), so mega/regional names
  resolve to the base entry when present.
- UI shows a turn-by-turn expander. Adds simulator tests. 59/59 passing.
